<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! face.hand.lifts ~ the hand reads the preview, names the row digest, and the lift signs

`kahua lift <title>` carries one staged row to every device the face wears: the second crossing of memory. It reads the staged row back first and prints its PREVIEW (title, row digest, fields, body, and whether a head already carries it), then lifts only on that row digest typed back at a terminal (its first eight hex), or on `--digest <hex>` naming the digest the preview printed. A bare `yes=true` names no digest and lifts nothing. A lift signs under the face's root, so a lift always asks the face's passphrase at a terminal; `--digest` spares the typed-back digest alone.

The lift names its taint list: `--taint none` when every input came from inside the face, else `--taint a,b`. A lift carries the staged row's own body and fields, so stage them first (`face.draft.stages`); a lift naming `--text`, `--file` or `--fields` refuses `kahua-lift-unstaged`. `--parent <cid>` names the revision it supersedes (`none` for a first lift), `--sources` further daemon sources the item distils (the staged row always rides), and `--proposal <id>` the proposal it answers: the proposal's body digest must equal the staged body's. Two digests share one word: the ROW digest (what `kahua stage` answers and a lift names) covers the row's body and fields, while a proposal's `digest` names the BODY digest, the body bytes alone.

The door re-reads the row at the act and refuses `kahua-lift-unstaged` (no such row) or `kahua-lift-digest-moved` (the row moved since the preview); a lift the head already carries lands nothing. The lift reads the lōkahi cap off the vessel's island and the operator's grant out of sealed custody, and refuses by name; an AI seat proposes and stages, and its session never lifts. `lares shore lift-kahua` lifts a different thing, the pending set a lay left behind (`carriage.draft.lifts`).

Under a pūlama the root signs at the pūlama's hand door, since the vessel there holds no face root: `--terms` runs every gate and prints ONE stdout line (the one unsigned act its root signs) and opens no route; the pūlama's `sign '<terms>'` checks it and signs; `--land '<answer>'` lands the signed record, where the door builds the act afresh and lands it only over a byte-equal body. Neither asks the passphrase on the vessel, and the host shim walks the pattern (`tools/lares-container.sh kahua lift|withdraw|carry`).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ preview-then-confirm · name-the-digest · a-pulama-hand

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`preview-then-confirm` params=`title/T taint/none face/1 ~ read the preview, then type the row digest's first eight hex back`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`name-the-digest` params=`title/T taint/none digest/<digest> proposal/<intent-id> face/1 ~ lift on the digest the preview printed, answering one proposal`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`a-pulama-hand` params=`title/T taint/none terms face/1 ~ print the one terms line a pūlama signs, opening no route`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ title · taint · digest · parent · sources · proposal · face · terms · land

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`title` params=`takes/title needs/required seat/1 as/<title> ~ the staged row's title`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`taint` params=`takes/tags needs/required ~ inputs from outside the face, comma-joined; 'none' where every input came from inside the face`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`digest` params=`takes/hex ~ the staged row's ROW digest, as its preview printed it; stands in for typing it back, and the passphrase prompt still needs a terminal`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`parent` params=`takes/cid ~ the revision this lift supersedes; 'none' for a first lift`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`sources` params=`takes/json ~ further daemon sources the item distils (the staged row always rides)`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`proposal` params=`takes/intent-id ~ the proposal this lift answers; its body digest must equal the staged body's`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`face` params=`takes/handle-index ~ which face's stage this call reads or writes, by persona index (a whole number from 0); absent, the one face standing open or the worn face`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`terms` params=`kind/switch ~ run every gate and print the one terms line a pūlama signs; opens no route and asks no passphrase here; name it or land=, never both`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`land` params=`takes/answer ~ land the signed record from a pūlama's sign answer; the door builds the act afresh and lands it only over a byte-equal body`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ hand

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`hand` params=`who/hand key/face-root ~ signs under the face's root out of sealed custody and always asks the face's passphrase at a terminal; a person runs it, an AI seat proposes and stages and names the command, and a bare yes=true lifts nothing`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/refuses`>>

!! refuses ~ kahua-lift-unconfirmed · kahua-lift-digest-moved · kahua-lift-unstaged · kahua-act-refused · ward-needs-tty · kahua-hand-malformed · face-malformed

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`kahua-lift-unconfirmed` params=`cure/[[face.hand.lifts title/T taint/none digest/<digest>]] ~ a lift needs eyes: name the digest the preview printed, or type it back at a terminal`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`kahua-lift-digest-moved` params=`cure/[[face.hand.lifts title/T taint/none]] ~ the staged row moved since the preview, or the digest named differs; read the preview again`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`kahua-lift-unstaged` params=`cure/[[face.draft.stages title/T text/<body>]] ~ no row stands staged at the title, or the line carried a body or fields: stage them first`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`kahua-act-refused` params=`cure/[[face.hand.lifts title/T taint/none]] ~ a lift names its taint: none, or a comma-joined list`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`ward-needs-tty` params=`~ the face's passphrase comes from a person at a terminal; --digest spares the typed-back digest alone`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`kahua-hand-malformed` params=`~ the pūlama's answer names the wrong kind, the wrong face, or both --terms and --land stood on one line`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`face-malformed` params=`~ --face names a persona index, a whole number from 0`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

